  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="c133d14f-dfe1-4d87-983d-a394d9d888d3"><problem><para>
      <para><emphasis>Select three</emphasis> quadratic expressions written in vertex form.</para>
      </para></problem><solution><para>["\\(y=(x-2)^2 + 1\\)", "\\(y=x^2 - 4\\)", "\\(y=(x-4)^2 + 6\\)"]</para><para>
      <para>The correct answers are: \(y=(x-2)^2 + 1, y=x^2 - 4, y=(x-4)^2 + 6\). </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
</document>
